Hi kpjeeja, thanks for your contribution!

One blocking comment from my side, consider: 
```
{
  "plugin": {
    "posix": {"active": true},
    "gds": {"active": false, "use_direct_io": false}
  }
}
```

With your current PR we promote the value of "use_direct_io" to the POSIX plugin, even if the POSIX plugin is chosen to run and would use by default O_DIRECT.  this seems wrong to me. However, Top-level to plugin level should be promoted, I agree on that one.

Then some minor comments:

* Given the many possible configuration options, I agree in general with the probe approach. It would be good to add a probe also for the non-direct path, we could run into permission issues for example.
* The requested bytes change is ok, the next version of NIXL will retry partial I/Os internally so it is not strictly necessary: https://github.com/ai-dynamo/nixl/pull/2224

